package engineadapter

// 范围建议与首次观察同次产生；原始观察仍须完整，选择不能伪装成非题目。
const recognitionImageScopePromptV1 = `
For this request use the image_scope_v1 extension. Keep ALL visible candidate questions in targets, including incidental or clipped neighboring questions. Do not erase them, mark them non_question, or solve them to decide scope. Add exactly one envelope field "scope":{"version":"image_scope_v1","source":"explicit|inferred","selected_orders":[1],"basis":"visible layout and user-scope evidence","dependencies":[{"for_orders":[1],"region":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":1,"height":1},"text":"verbatim visible shared material"}],"excluded":[{"order":2,"reason":"specific visible reason this candidate is incidental"}]}.
Orders are ONE-BASED original targets array positions, not printed numbers or invented IDs. Every candidate must occur exactly once in selected_orders OR excluded. selected_orders must be nonempty. Explicit current page/section/question scope takes priority over composition. Task action (solve/grade) is independent of scope; handwriting or blank space alone does not identify the intended questions. When scope is unspecified, use the main page, complete coherent question group, printed hierarchy, section boundaries and referenced materials to infer the intended task. A newly starting section or a neighboring page fragment is evidence, not an automatic exclusion rule. Do not always reduce a full worksheet to a few questions. Do not silently expand an ambiguous request to all visible pages.
dependencies are only the visible examples, parent passages, diagrams or conditions actually needed by selected targets; attach each to its actual for_orders, never count or solve materials as extra questions. Include their exact visible text and original-page pixel rectangle; use [] if none. Preserve clipped glyphs as unresolved risks; do not complete from memory, textbook answers, arithmetic or handwriting. Keep source observations unchanged. Any missing required instruction, number, negation or student handwriting remains uncertain.
When selected content is genuinely clipped or unreadable, also add scope.gaps=[{"order":1,"kind":"quotation|instruction|condition|handwriting","before":"exact visible text immediately before gap","after":"exact visible text immediately after gap"}]. Include only actual gaps, never normal exercise fill-in blanks or intentional ellipses. Keep each anchor verbatim and at most 80 characters. Do not propose missing text in these anchors. If the ONLY source uncertainty is a declared quotation, instruction or condition gap, use the corresponding typed risk: source_gap_quotation, source_gap_instruction or source_gap_condition. All other uncertainties must retain their own risks and appropriate gap kinds. A missing exercise instruction is not a missing quotation. Omit gaps or use [] when no actual missing source exists. The extension does not permit other extra fields in targets.`
